    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0614" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.124/303.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-08-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 18, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Government knows nothing of changes referred to by Ecuadorean Minister. The
                    matter has not been bought before Congress. Companies mentioned bid about the
                    time MacArthur. All bids must be made blindly, as there is no contractor capable
                    of preparing intelligent plan. Economy or ability of Americans will not affect
                    the award. I have received from the Minister for Foreign Affairs a reply to my
                    protest, saying that nothing further will be done until the special commissioner
                    now in Europe seeking bids returns.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
